::: {.doc-subject}

Map every node of a depth-first search tree to its children.
:::

::: {.doc-usage-source}
Usage

[Source](https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase/blob/main/python/edgecase/graph.py#L47977-L48034){target="_blank" rel="noopener"}
:::

::: {.doc-signature .doc-Kind.FUNCTION}
```python
Graph.dfs_successors(
    source=None,
    depth_limit=None,
    mode="out",
)
```
:::

::: {.doc-text}

![DFS successors](/assets/graphs/dfs-successors.light.svg){.lightbox fig-alt="The same four-node tree searched depth-first from A (outlined). Each accent arrow points from a parent to a child it discovered, and numbered badges give the visit order A, B, C, D. The card maps A to its children B and D, and B to C." width="100%"}

The reverse view of `dfs_predecessors()`: for each node of the depth-first search tree
(or forest) that has children, the nodes discovered from it, in discovery order.
:::

## Parameters {.doc-parameters}

::: {.doc-definition-items}
<code>[source]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [Union[int, str, None]]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [None]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>

:   Optional start node (ID or label). If `None` (default), every component is searched.

<code>[depth_limit]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [int | None]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [None]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>

:   Optional maximum depth.

<code>[mode]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [str]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [[&quot;out&quot;]{.st}]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>

:   Edge direction to follow on directed graphs: `"out"` (default), `"in"` or `"all"`.
:::

## Returns {.doc-returns}

::: {.doc-definition-items}
<code> [dict[int, list[int]]]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>

:   Parent node ID to its children.
:::

## Raises {.doc-raises}

::: {.doc-definition-items}
<code> [ValueError]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>

:   If the source does not exist or `mode` is invalid.
:::

## Technical Notes {.doc-technical-notes}

Grouped from the tree edges of `dfs_edges()`. Matches NetworkX's `dfs_successors`.

## Examples {.doc-examples}

::: {#8c5eba44 .cell execution_count=1}
``` {.python .cell-code}
import edgecase as ec

g = ec.Graph().add_nodes(["A", "B", "C", "D"])
g.add_edges([("A", "B"), ("B", "C"), ("A", "D")])

{g.get_label_from_id(p): [g.get_label_from_id(c) for c in cs]
 for p, cs in g.dfs_successors("A").items()}
```

::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=1}
```
{'A': ['B', 'D'], 'B': ['C']}
```
:::
:::
